# Two different rules apply here and mixing them up is how a required
# deliverable gets excluded from a cold clone.
#
# SCRATCH FILES that share a name with something a product might legitimately
# commit are ANCHORED with a leading slash. A pattern with no slash matches at
# ANY depth: a bare `junit.xml` in a product .gitignore once silently excluded
# a required committed fixture elsewhere in this mission, and a cold clone then
# failed every test while the build machine passed. fixtures/population.tle,
# fixtures/divergence_dataset.npz, screenshots/*.png and
# validation/*_output.txt are REQUIRED committed deliverables and nothing here
# may match them; tests/test_regressions.py checks that, implementing the
# matching itself because `git check-ignore` exits 0 when a NEGATION pattern
# matches and a check that read only its exit status would report a
# deliberately re-included file as ignored.
#
# TOOL CACHES are deliberately UNANCHORED, because they appear wherever the
# tool was invoked. Running `ruff check` from inside src/orbitdrift leaves a
# src/orbitdrift/.ruff_cache that an anchored /.ruff_cache/ would not catch,
# and it was committed once before this comment was written.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
/.coverage
/htmlcov/
/junit.xml
